Chapter: RangeRefineIf

 Branch refinement in the middle end: a plain Integer
 parameter stored into a 0..255 field is provable ONLY from the
 comparisons guarding the store - `0 <= i` (name on the right) and
 `i < 200` (name on the left) refine i to 0..199 inside the inner
 then arm. Before refinement this store was the CDX2051 unproven
 error; with it the flow draws the CDX2053 proven info the sidecar
 pins. The leak twin lives in errors/range-refine-else-leak.

Section: Definitions

  Entry = record {
   code : Integer between 0 and 255
  }

  clamp-code : Integer -> Integer
  clamp-code (i) =
   if 0 <= i
   then if i < 200 then (Entry { code = i }).code else 0
   else 0

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   print-line-uni (integer-to-text (clamp-code 45))
  end
